================================================================================
Note on MySQL Connector/J
================================================================================

At run time this gem links MySQL Connector/J (the `com.mysql:mysql-connector-j`
JDBC driver) and calls its Java API directly, so a program combining the two is
a combined work in the sense of the GNU GPL.

Connector/J is distributed by Oracle under a dual license:

  * the GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2) *only*, together with the
    "Universal FOSS Exception, version 1.0"; or
  * a separate commercial license from Oracle.

This gem is licensed under GPLv2 *only* — the same version Connector/J uses.

Accordingly:

  * This gem's own source (lib/, ext/) is licensed GPLv2-only; see COPYING
  * Connector/J is NOT bundled or redistributed by this gem.  It is declared as
    an external requirement and obtained separately (e.g. `rake connector`, or
    from Maven Central / Oracle).  Connector/J remains under its own license
    (GPLv2 + Universal FOSS Exception, or Oracle commercial); this project does
    not, and cannot, relicense it

Reproducing mysql2's Ruby API is an interface reimplementation and does not make
this a derivative of the upstream mysql2 gem (MIT-licensed).
